  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nIn MDN we're trying to find a definition for the [top level traversable](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/document-sequences.html#nav-top) that is understandable to website developers and not just browser implementers.\r\nCould we have a normative definition added to the spec that we can reference? \r\n\r\nThe context of the discussion is where this term is used to describe that there can only be one Document picture-in-picture window per top level traversable. We're currently using \"browser tab\" but  [there is some discussion](https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/31016#issuecomment-1862096293) as to whether \"page\" is better. ",
